# Egress allowlist applied to every agent container (Claude and Codex).
# Formerly split into claude.allowlist / codex.allowlist, which each
# @include'd this file and appended agent-specific endpoints; consolidated
# into this single deny-by-default list so all containers share one file
# (#1420). Egress is the union of every agent's endpoints on every container.
# Syntax: one hostname per line. Blank lines and comments are ignored.
# Each host carries an inline triage rationale; see
# docs/runbooks/devcontainer-tool-network-triage.md and the
# scripts/scan_allowlist_rationale.py gate.
github.com  # Git remote operations and web endpoints for the repository host.
api.github.com  # GitHub REST/GraphQL API used by gh and GitHub MCP tools at runtime.
api.mcp.github.com  # GitHub remote MCP server endpoint used by the GitHub MCP tools.
objects.githubusercontent.com  # GitHub-hosted object/LFS blobs fetched by gh and installers.
raw.githubusercontent.com  # Raw file fetch for GitHub-hosted scripts and configs.
docs.github.com  # GitHub product documentation fetched as a primary source during agent lookups; public read-only docs, no secrets sent.
release-assets.githubusercontent.com  # GitHub release assets (apm Nix derivation, pinned binaries).
pypi.org  # Python package index metadata for uv dependency resolution.
files.pythonhosted.org  # Python wheel/sdist downloads for uv sync.
astral.sh  # uv installer/redirect host for the pinned uv release.
static.crates.io  # Rust crate downloads for cargo build dependencies.
index.crates.io  # Rust crate registry sparse index.
cache.nixos.org  # Nix binary cache for substituting build outputs.
channels.nixos.org  # Nixpkgs channel metadata for flake inputs.
github-releases.githubusercontent.com  # GitHub release binary downloads used by installers.
ghcr.io  # GitHub Container Registry pulls for the prebuilt devcontainer images.
mcr.microsoft.com  # Microsoft Container Registry for base image and feature layers.
aka.ms  # Microsoft redirect host historically required by the official microsoft/apm installer; see #800 (necessity disputed, candidate for re-triage).
# Threat-intelligence feeds queried by scripts/threat_intel_triage.py scan (#1277).
api.osv.dev  # OSV.dev vulnerability feed (querybatch/query/vulns) correlated against locked dependencies by the threat-intel triage scan.
www.cisa.gov  # CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog feed used by the threat-intel triage scan to flag known-exploited findings.
api.first.org  # FIRST EPSS exploit-prediction scores enriching threat-intel triage findings (advisory-only per #173).
services.nvd.nist.gov  # NVD CVE metadata enriching threat-intel triage findings already surfaced by OSV/GHSA (supplemental per #174).
# Agent runtime API endpoints. Consolidated from the former per-agent
# claude.allowlist / codex.allowlist (#1420); admitted on every container.
api.anthropic.com  # Anthropic API endpoint used by the Claude CLI at runtime.
docs.anthropic.com  # Anthropic API/model documentation and changelog fetched as a primary source during agent lookups (#1429); public read-only docs, no secrets sent.
cdn.prod.website-files.com  # Webflow CDN (Cloudflare-fronted) serving Anthropic "Zero Trust for AI Agents" eBook PDF; read-only public GET re-grounds the parent #178 premise from a primary source (#1383); no credentials sent.
api.openai.com  # OpenAI API endpoint used by the Codex CLI at runtime.
platform.openai.com  # OpenAI API/model/pricing documentation fetched as a primary source during agent lookups (#1429); public read-only docs, no secrets sent.
auth.openai.com  # ChatGPT-mediated OAuth token exchange during `codex login`.
# Vendor-neutral security guidance fetched as a primary source during agent lookups.
genai.owasp.org  # OWASP GenAI Security Project (OWASP Foundation): public read-only LLM/GenAI security guidance (Top 10 for LLM Applications, Agentic AI) fetched as a primary source during agent lookups (#1487); no secrets sent.
